            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:grammar-fill:1",
            "text": "“If you have ever suffered for my sweetness, I’m willing to live as you wish...” The chorus of As You Wish resounded at the Temple of Heaven and passers-by were surprised to find this Chinese song was performed by a US choir（合唱团）, One Voice Children’s Choir. Their infectious singing was recorded in a video and became an instant hit on social media."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:grammar-fill:2",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:grammar-fill:2",
            "text": "Fukuda, the conductor, introduced One Voice was just singing casually when people gathered around, and the video subsequently spread online. “Despite different cultures, we can still relate to those same messages. I hope no matter what people are going through, the song will touch them.” said Fukuda."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:grammar-fill:3",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:grammar-fill:3",
            "text": "The choir, with its mission to inspire the world through children’s voices, consists of a group of children who met while singing at the 2002 Salt Lake City Winter Olympics. In addition to As You Wish, Tomorrow Will Be Better is also a signature song of them. They’ve just completed their China tour, with performances in several cities."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:grammar-fill:4",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hebei-shijiazhuang-2025-m1:grammar-fill:4",
            "text": "During their final performance in China, Fukuda and the children teared up, continuously waving goodbye to the audience. “The warm welcome from the Chinese people moved us deeply. I really felt connected to the audience,” Fukuda remarked. “Although I don’t know them, I felt that our message was received by them.”"
          }
